# ── TBC Anniversary TOC ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Interface 20506 = Burning Crusade Classic & Classic Anniversary Edition
# (per Warcraft Wiki current-interface table). Matched by TBC clients ahead of
# the generic ToonAge.toc fallback.
#
# Scope: advisory only (stat caps, weapon skill, cap-aware gear). No guide /
# navigation engine on TBC — the player uses Zygor for questing. See
# Docs/CLASSIC_ANNIVERSARY_BRIEF.md.
#
# This TOC lists the SHARED, flavor-neutral Core engine plus (from Task 7) the
# TBC-specific Data/TBC/* and TBC modules. It deliberately lists NO Data/Retail/
# file and NO retail-only module: the flavor gate in Core/Profile.lua (tbc
# profile) is the runtime backstop, and this TOC is the packaging backstop, so a
# TBC install ships only TBC content. StatEngine.lua is retail-DR-specific and
# is intentionally absent — TBC uses hard stat caps (Data/TBC), not DR curves.

# ── Libraries ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Libs\LibStub.lua
Libs\WagoAnalytics\Shim.lua

# ── Core Framework (SHARED — flavor-neutral) ───────────────────────────
